{
  "dom_id": "step-q67893",
  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "What is the measure of each interior angle of a regular polygon with $16$ sides?",
  "worked_solution": "A regular polygon with $16$ sides has all its interior angles with the same measure.\n\nThe sum of the measures of its interior angles is \n\n$$\n{180}^{∘}\\times (16-2)=2\\,{520}^{∘}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the measure of each interior angle is \n\n$$\n\\frac{2\\,{520}^{∘}}{16}={157.5}^{∘}.\n$$",
